{"id": "ef1293a9-ada5-4405-aa1c-d894fad596f9", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T00:29:53.026930", "source": "user", "parent_id": "cce10c27-fd12-41ed-8bbc-5bbfe8cac84f", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only deliverable (no execution). For the initial inspection, please provide: (1) a brief inspection of any input files or repository material under /workspace (e.g., track.md or related docs) and a summary of what constraints they impose; (2) a proposed approach for the experiment design that directly addresses the question — Does scaling llama-2-70b vs llama-2-13b necessarily improve performance, or can insufficient pre-training and the lack of refined alignment negate the benefits of a larger parameter count? Specifically identify the candidate model set (e.g., the Llama-2 family at 7B/13B/70B, plus a relevant 'insufficient pretraining' baseline such as an undertrained checkpoint, and a 'no refined alignment' baseline such as a base-only or early-instruct checkpoint), the controlled variables (token count, tokenizer, context, decoding settings, evaluation prompts, hardware/precision, prompt template), the independent variable (model scale vs. pretraining/alignment tier), the dependent variables (benchmark and human-eval scores, plus calibration/hallucination/safety proxies), the evaluation suite, the analysis plan (scaling-law ablation, ceiling/floor effects, alignment-vs-scale decomposition, confound checks), and the feasibility assessment (data availability, compute, runtime, access to checkpoints). (3) List consequential assumptions and uncertainties — for example: what counts as 'refined alignment' in this context (RLHF vs. SFT vs. instruction tuning vs. DPO), how to operationalize 'insufficient pretraining' (token budget truncated run vs. compute-matched smaller model), whether comparisons are at fixed inference budget, and which evaluation signals are sensitive enough to detect alignment effects at frontier scale. Do not provide the final solution yet — only the proposed approach and these clarifications.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does increasing model size (as in comparing llama-2-70b to llama-2-13b) necessarily yield improved performance, or can insufficient pre-training and a lack of refined alignment negate the benefits of a larger parameter count?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
