{"id": "b55e0e99-37a1-4ebd-bc3f-d3f511012674", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T00:32:18.832379", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1fb69010-15aa-4f6f-a098-301137886dfd", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with the following resolutions to the open assumptions/uncertainties — these are your working defaults for the full design, no further clarification round needed unless an execution-blocking constraint appears later. Brief rationale and one or two source-cited anchors are expected in each design section; status as design-only is preserved (no runs, all numbers as 'to be measured' or cited from published reports with stable identifiers/version pins). Working defaults: (A1) Llama-2 family only — primary matrix is {7B, 13B, 70B} base and Chat, with 34B-Chat included as a published data point where it strengthens the scaling curve; (A2) 'refined alignment' = Llama-2-Chat full recipe (SFT + iterative RLHF + rejection sampling); base models are the 'no refined alignment' baseline and SFT-only checkpoints (where released by Meta or reproducible third parties) are treated as a secondary contrast within the alignment tier; (A3) operationalize insufficient pretraining on two legs and report both — (3a) same-architecture reduced-token run using publicly reported scaling-law points or third-party undertrained checkpoints (e.g., from Pythia/RedPajama-style suites at matched architecture) and (3b) compute-equivalent smaller model trained longer (Chinchilla reallocation); if (3a) is not available for the Llama-2 family, flag the limitation explicitly and lean on scaling-law extrapolation anchored to published 7B/13B/70B points; (A4) primary comparisons at fixed inference FLOPs per generated token (so quantization/decoding don't masquerade as scale effects), with at-recommended-precision post-hoc reported as a confound-check annex (U3); (A5) primary alignment detectors at frontier scale are AlpacaEval-2 win-rate, IFEval, and a help-harm tradeoff curve on HarmBench/BBQ-style prompts; MMLU, GSM8K, HumanEval, BBH, MATH serve only as capability sanity checks; (A6) adopt the pre-registered decision rule you described, but tighten the headline criterion to require both capability non-significance on ≥2/4 capability benchmarks after Holm correction AND Δ_alignment collapse (≤50% of the 13B gap, with bootstrap CI on the within-prompt Delta) on ≥2/3 alignment-sensitive metrics, before concluding '70B ≥ 13B is not necessary'. Additional resolutions: (U2) report safety as BOTH a combined help-harm tradeoff curve (positive alignment component, AUC over refusal-vs-helpfulness) AND per-benchmark scores on HarmBench, ToxiGen, BBQ, TruthfulQA-gen — no single-number reduction; (U4) primary matrix stays Llama-2; Llama-3 (8B/70B/405B base and Instruct, if cited) appears only in framing/positioning, never in experimental cells; (U5) primary analysis bf16, plus a 70B bf16-vs-int4-GPTQ confound cell on a capability and an alignment benchmark (paper both); (U6) include the ~200-prompt double-blind human-eval subset with ≥3 raters/prompt and Krippendorff α ≥ 0.7, but mark it as in-scope for the design and only lightweight execution if compute allows. Now produce the full design deliverable with: (i) complete experiment matrix (every cell, every level, checkpoint identifier/version), (ii) fixed controlled-variable table with exact values, (iii) per-benchmark protocol (prompt template, n-shot, sampling, scorer, version pin), (iv) statistical analysis plan executing the six steps above with explicit test names, corrections, power/MDE for the headline test, (v) feasibility and compute estimate table per cell, (vi) confounds and limitations section that explicitly handles partial-checkpoint unavailability and quantization drift, and (vii) a brief rationale per design choice grounded in cited sources. Do not invent fact IDs; where you cite a number or claim, attach the source identifier so a reviewer can locate it.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 24}
